WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.300
 Installing a pool above
ground costs much less

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.430
than installing one in-ground.

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.640
This is because there's
no excavation required.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.920
You can build an elevated
deck around the top

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.780
to give it an
in-ground appearance,

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.930
or you can simply climb up
a ladder and jump right in.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:31.270
No hole to dig, no
underground pipes to install.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:34.210
Just a day or so of
on-site prep and assembly,

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.830
and you can take to your
above-ground pool like a duck

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:37.630
to water.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.910
At the factory, a
computer-guided machine

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:47.050
cuts vinyl panels for the pool's
water retaining inside surface.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:50.270
The vinyl comes in a wide
choice of printed designs.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.710
It's tear resistant, UV
resistant, and is treated

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:55.240
with an antifungal coating.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.160
The wall panel is rectangular,
and the floor panels are curved

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.600
to fit the pool's perimeter.

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:05.269
The wall panels go
through a welder that

00:01:05.269 --> 00:01:07.280
fuses a bead to the top edge.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:12.550
A bead is a flexible
U-shaped thermoplastic strip

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:15.250
that is used to attach the
pool wall to the liner.

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:21.560
A hot welding tool slightly
melts both the bead

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:24.180
and the liner edge, so when
they cool and solidify,

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:24.980
they're bonded.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:30.930
The liner is ready
to be assembled.

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:33.900
Workers use a manual welding
machine that generates

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.640
heat with radio frequencies.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:39.960
They overlap the edges
of adjoining panels,

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.220
then fuse them together.

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.900
After connecting the floor
panels to each other,

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:48.855
workers complete the liner by
joining the wall to the floor.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:54.750
A quality control inspector
checks every soldered seam

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:55.875
to make sure they're solid.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:02.130
Meanwhile, workers
manufacture the pool's

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:03.420
structural components.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.130
They feed a continuous strip
of painted galvanized steel

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:09.370
through a roll former.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.760
The strip is shaped
to a specific profile.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.120
A punch press cuts
the components to

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.520
the required length and shape.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:24.150
Four different structural
components are made this way.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:26.040
The pieces that form
the top and bottom

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.160
tracks of the pool, the
vertical posts that support

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.620
the pool wall, and
the ledges running

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:32.900
along the top of the wall.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:37.935
The wall is also made of
painted galvanized steel.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:42.300
A roller impresses a corrugated
pattern to give the wall

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.285
more vertical strength.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:47.250
Then, a press punches out
openings for the pool's

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.435
water inlet and filter.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:53.140
After folding each end
of the wall over itself

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:56.440
to form a strong edge, they
punch holes for the bolts

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.460
that will join the edges.

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:03.220
A stamping die
progressively shapes strips

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:06.010
of galvanized steel
into connectors.

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:08.800
The connectors join the vertical
posts to the structure's

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.420
bottom track and top rail.

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:15.190
An injection molder makes
the plastic covers that will

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:16.540
hide those connectors.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.870
Workers then box the liner
and structural components

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:24.000
for transport to the
installation site.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.960
On site, they lay crushed
stone around the perimeter

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.540
to support the bottom track
under the weight of the water.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.920
Next, they unroll the
pool wall and place it

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:44.820
in the bottom track.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.290
They place a vertical post
over each bottom connector

00:03:58.290 --> 00:03:59.430
and secure it with screws.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:05.390
Inside the pool wall, they
lay down a base of sand

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:06.290
and compact it.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.875
Then, they lay down
landscaping fabric.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.730
They cut a hole for a
central bottom drain.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.204
Then they began
spreading out the liner.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:28.810
They hook the bead over
the top edge of the wall,

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:30.970
then lock it in place
with the top rail.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.060
Once the liner is
fully attached,

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:37.940
they suction out the air to
draw it tight against the wall.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:41.510
They seal the liner
to the bottom drain.

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:46.330
They hide the top
rail under the ledge,

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:48.205
and the connections
under plastic caps.

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:54.425
They run pipes to connect the
filtration system and skimmer.

00:04:57.910 --> 00:05:00.280
Then, with an
ordinary garden hose,

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:03.150
they fill the pool with water.

